From: Spaced Linux Developers <dev@spacedlinux.com>
Subject: ezoom: let the wheel grab step aside for keyboard shortcuts

Patch 0001 takes a screen-wide grab for the Shift+Super chord alone, and patch
0002 releases it for the duration of a press on a button that is not a wheel
button. A key shortcut is not a button: after a Fire Writing stroke ends, the
chord is still held and 0002 takes the wheel grab back, so Shift+Print still
produces no image while the fire burns. mate-screenshot selects its area with
an X pointer and keyboard grab (mate-utils screenshot-utils.c gdk_seat_grab),
and the X server keeps one grab at a time, so its request returns
GrabAlreadyGrabbed while Compiz holds one.

Release the wheel grab for a key press and key release. Wheel suppression is
unchanged: the button paths added by 0001 and 0002 take the grab back, and a
wheel press is a button press.

--- a/src/ezoom/ezoom.c
+++ b/src/ezoom/ezoom.c
@@ -2509,6 +2509,24 @@
         }
     }
 
+    /* Spaced: a keyboard shortcut may launch an external tool that needs a
+     * pointer and keyboard grab of its own (Shift+Print runs mate-screenshot).
+     * The X server keeps one grab at a time, so the wheel grab must step aside
+     * for the whole key action; the button paths above take it back. */
+    if (event->type == KeyPress || event->type == KeyRelease)
+    {
+        s = findScreenAtDisplay (d, ((XKeyEvent *) event)->root);
+        if (s)
+        {
+            ZOOM_SCREEN (s);
+            if (zs->wheelGrabIndex)
+            {
+                removeScreenGrab (s, zs->wheelGrabIndex, NULL);
+                zs->wheelGrabIndex = 0;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     switch (event->type) {
 	case MotionNotify:
 	    mev =  (XMotionEvent *) event;
